e Rings of power there  were surprisingly not a lot of rings in  total the rings of Power are comprised  of 20. the three we saw for the elves  seven for the dwarves nine for Mortal  men and the one ring to rule them all in  the book the first to be created were  the ones given to the dwarves and Men it  was only after Sauron left a region that  kellebrimbor went on to forge the three  rings we see in the show so I wonder how  the writers will address this next  season it's not until 10 years later  that Sauron will create the One Ring  however considering the show has played  fast and loose with the timeline we'll  likely see this happening well before  them as the Rings are forward you can  even see the molten lava form the eye of  Sauron showing the Ring's connection to  the dark lord according to the book it  is Galadriel kirtan and gilgalad who are  the original bearers of these Elven  rings with gilgalad later giving his  ring to elrond each ring represents an  element Fire Water and Air which are  represented by these colored gems not in  the book is galadriel's dagger which  once belonged to her brother it'll be  melted down to fuse with the mithril in  making the Rings the Rings then become a  physical manifestation of both Sauron  and Galadriel sauron's Power and  galadriel's Light the expeditionary  force that set out from numenor has  arrived home to a sad sight black flags  Adorn the harbor which means the king is  dead before his death Chancellor R  farazon commissioned draftsman and some  apprentices including Ellendale's  daughter aaryan to draw the king but  during her meeting with him he grabs her  arm thinking she's his daughter stating  that if the old ways of their people are  not stored their Island will fall he's  referring to how the numenoreans once  were friends with the elves which they  now look on with disgust Aryan also  discovers the king's palantir an object  whose chronic use made the king unable  to separate what is and was and will